    "Through this conversion, traditionally dated to 301, Armenia became the first kingdom in history to adopt Christianity as its state religion. Gregory was consecrated bishop and organized the Armenian Church's hierarchy, founding the see of Echmiadzin, which remains the spiritual center of the Armenian Apostolic Church.",
