    "With this new alphabet, Mesrop led a team of scholars and disciples in translating the Bible and patristic texts into Armenian, inaugurating what is often called the 'Golden Age' of Armenian literature, and he personally undertook missionary journeys to spread literacy and the Gospel throughout Armenia and neighboring Georgia and Caucasian Albania.",
