    "Subjected to brutal torture for refusing to renounce Christianity, tradition recounts that she was swallowed by a demonic dragon in her prison cell and, making the sign of the cross, burst forth unharmed, becoming thereafter a popular subject of iconography and protection invoked especially during childbirth.",
